1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,488
qnxdoctor checks a QNX SDP 8.0 Makefile from
the host.

2
00:00:04,488 --> 00:00:08,775
This demo uses the bundled examples and a
fake toolchain.

3
00:00:08,775 --> 00:00:11,776
No board, no QEMU, and no SDP.

4
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:18,687
Version prints 0.1.0, the same string as the
report header.

5
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:24,697
The demo command runs all three examples.

6
00:00:24,697 --> 00:00:29,334
hello-sdp8 and plain-aarch64 pass in
degraded mode: the files are fine, and a

7
00:00:29,334 --> 00:00:31,475
missing qcc is only a warning.

8
00:00:31,475 --> 00:00:33,258
broken-port is the expected failure.

9
00:00:33,258 --> 00:00:35,399
The demo command still exits 0.

10
00:00:35,399 --> 00:00:37,896
It is a gallery, not a gate.

11
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:48,569
Diagnosing broken-port directly exits 1.

12
00:00:48,569 --> 00:00:53,306
The recap at the bottom is the part to read.

13
00:00:53,306 --> 00:00:58,518
common.mk forces gcc, passes march native,
and still points at qnx710.

14
00:00:58,518 --> 00:00:59,939
qtargets.mk is missing.

15
00:00:59,939 --> 00:01:05,624
nto-armv7-o-le is not an SDP 8.0 CPU, and
nto-aarch64-o-be asks for big-endian.

16
00:01:05,624 --> 00:01:11,783
net.c includes a Linux header and epoll, and
it calls socket without libsocket.

17
00:01:11,783 --> 00:01:16,047
The shell script and the workflow never
source qnxsdp-env.sh.

18
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:25,060
Sourcing demo/mock-env.sh builds a fake SDP
tree: qcc and q++ stubs, plus qconfig.mk,

19
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:26,643
qtargets.mk, and recurse.mk.

20
00:01:26,643 --> 00:01:29,809
The stub is not a compiler.

21
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:34,119
The same hello project is now mode ready.

22
00:01:34,119 --> 00:01:40,488
QNX_HOST and QNX_TARGET resolve, PATH finds
the stub qcc, and qcc -V reports

23
00:01:40,488 --> 00:01:41,958
gcc_ntoaarch64le and gcc_ntox86_64.

24
00:01:41,958 --> 00:01:46,858
The project checks are unchanged, so the run
still passes.

25
00:01:46,858 --> 00:01:49,797
This is not a Neutrino boot.

26
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:53,003
With --require-sdp, those missing-toolchain
warnings become errors.

27
00:01:53,003 --> 00:01:56,607
hello-sdp8 now fails, even though the
Makefiles are clean.

28
00:01:56,607 --> 00:02:01,413
Use that flag on a build job that must have
the SDK.

29
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:08,349
JSON is the same report: status, mode,
findings, and passed checks.

30
00:02:08,349 --> 00:02:11,366
Scripts can read it without scraping the
text.

31
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,517
Warnings do not fail the process.

32
00:02:18,517 --> 00:02:19,289
Errors do.

33
00:02:19,289 --> 00:02:22,378
qnxdoctor reads files and does not run
recipes.

34
00:02:22,378 --> 00:02:26,625
It has not been tested on real SDP hardware
or QEMU.

